With unlimited buy/sell pairs allowed (buy and sell on the same day is fine, no cooldown, no fee), the optimal strategy simplifies to: capture every single profitable up-move.

```python
def max_profit_unlimited(prices):
    profit = 0
    for i in range(1, len(prices)):
        if prices[i] > prices[i - 1]:
            profit += prices[i] - prices[i - 1]
    return profit
```

This works because any multi-day gain can be decomposed into its daily up-moves with no loss — buying at the start of an upward run and selling at the end earns exactly the sum of each day's gain along the way, and unlimited transactions mean there's no cost to slicing a big win into many small ones.
